# AI gateway rules

- Vimla owns an `AiProvider` abstraction. ProxyAPI is the first adapter, not the domain API.
- Provider model IDs must not leak throughout product code. Map Vimla model IDs to provider IDs in catalog/configuration.
- Model metadata/capabilities/pricing must be versionable and configurable.
- Separate capabilities: text/chat, image, video, audio, embeddings, tool use. Do not force all providers into one lossy method if capability-specific interfaces are clearer.
- Provider credentials are server-side only.
- Every provider call requires an existing usage reservation unless the operation is explicitly free/internal.
- Capture request ID, provider, model/version, token/media usage, latency, status and actual/derived provider cost for accounting/observability.
- Streaming text should stream through Vimla backend; provider streams are never exposed as raw privileged connections.
- Add timeouts, controlled retries and retry classification. Do not retry non-idempotent expensive operations blindly.
- Auto-routing is a later feature. Keep routing decisions separate from UI and provider adapters.
